  "section_notes": "The final S2 gives exact per-model failure rates to prospective customers and keeps them confidential from the public, which satisfies HC-1 and NW-1, but it contains no mandatory sales stop, so a model above 5% can keep selling pending regulator action (favouring Northwind's Hearth 10). S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S1 reports serious incidents within 24 hours but only annually summarises other incidents, and S3's new-unit deadline of 24 months exceeds the 12-month benchmark."
